# The indexer image is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT (`docker build -f indexer/Dockerfile .`,
# see make images, ci.yml and cd.yml), because the Job needs corpus/fetch.py, sources.yaml,
# MANIFEST.md and eval/fixtures. Docker reads the ignore file of the build context, so the
# one that applies is /.dockerignore, an allowlist of exactly what the Dockerfile copies.
#
# This file only matters if someone builds with indexer/ as the context. The Dockerfile then
# fails at its first COPY of corpus/, which is the right outcome. Until it does, it keeps the
# same junk out of that context.
.git
__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
tests
requirements-dev.txt
corpus
.env
.env.*
